.TH HADOFIX 1 "2026-09" "hadofix" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
hadofix \- apply the fixes hadolint asks for
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hadofix
.I DOCKERFILE
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Not a linter:
.BR hadolint (1)
is the engine.
.B hadofix
runs
.B hadolint \-\-format json
over
.IR DOCKERFILE ,
rewrites it for the findings whose fix is mechanical, and lists every finding
it will not guess at.
.PP
The unified diff goes to standard output and the report to standard error, so
the diff can be piped and nothing is written unless
.B \-\-write
is given. Each hunk carries a
.B # hadofix(RULE):
comment explaining why the change is right.
.PP
hadolint's own configuration decides what is considered: a rule ignored in
.I .hadolint.yaml
or by an inline pragma is never fixed.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-write
Apply the diff in place.
.TP
.BI \-\-from\-json " PATH"
Read
.B hadolint \-\-format json
output from
.I PATH
.RB ( \- " for standard input)"
instead of running hadolint.
.TP
.BI \-\-hadolint " BIN"
The hadolint binary to run. Defaults to
.B hadolint
on
.BR PATH .
.TP
.B \-\-resolve\-digests
Let DL3006 and DL3007 pin a base image to a content digest. Docker Hub only,
and needs network access.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Clean: hadolint found nothing, or everything it found was fixed and written.
.TP
.B 1
Findings remain \- some were refused, or the diff was printed and not applied.
.TP
.B 2
Bad command line.
.TP
.B 66
The Dockerfile does not exist.
.TP
.B 69
hadolint is not installed, or its output could not be read.
.TP
.B 74
The Dockerfile exists but could not be read.
.TP
.B 77
Permission denied.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
See what would change:
.PP
.RS
.B hadofix Dockerfile
.RE
.PP
Apply it:
.PP
.RS
.B hadofix Dockerfile \-\-write
.RE
.PP
Reuse hadolint output you already have:
.PP
.RS
.B hadolint \-f json Dockerfile | hadofix Dockerfile \-\-from\-json \-
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR docker (1),
.BR hadolint (1).
Project documentation:
https://github.com/fabiocicerchia/hadofix
.SH RULES
.PP
Rules named
.B DL####
are hadolint's. Rules named
.B HF####
are hadofix's own: shell-form ENTRYPOINT/CMD and what it costs at
.BR "docker stop" " (HF1001),"
an entrypoint script that never calls
.B exec
(HF1002), a forking process with no init (HF1003), and a final stage that never
leaves root (HF1004).
